WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.627 --> 00:00:03.002
All right.

00:00:03.002 --> 00:00:04.129
Here we go.

00:00:04.129 --> 00:00:07.090
[upbeat music]

00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:14.597
My name's Daryl Smith.

00:00:14.597 --> 00:00:16.599
My name is Preston Smith.

00:00:16.599 --> 00:00:18.268
I'm the scientific glass blower.

00:00:18.643 --> 00:00:22.063
I'm the senior scientific
glassblower at Yale University

00:00:22.063 --> 00:00:23.815
housed in the chemistry
department.

00:00:24.399 --> 00:00:26.735
They opened the shop in 1924.

00:00:27.777 --> 00:00:30.572
It's very critical for research
to have somebody on site.

00:00:31.364 --> 00:00:34.743 align:end position:100% line:0%
There's a vast variety
of scientific glassware

00:00:34.743 --> 00:00:36.119 align:start size:66% position:34% line:0%
that researchers use.

00:00:36.161 --> 00:00:37.328
They're doing unique research,

00:00:37.328 --> 00:00:39.205
so sometimes it takes
unique glassware.

00:00:39.539 --> 00:00:41.332
Some of it's standard
catalog items,

00:00:41.332 --> 00:00:43.793
some of it's modifications
of a standard item,

00:00:43.793 --> 00:00:45.503
and sometimes it's
a very unique design.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:47.797
I had this novelty

00:00:47.797 --> 00:00:50.717
item called bubble machine
where the liquid goes through

00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:52.302
the air return captures

00:00:52.302 --> 00:00:52.969
some of the liquid

00:00:52.969 --> 00:00:54.512
and it goes up
through a small tube,

00:00:54.512 --> 00:00:57.599
so I incorporated that
into a wine decanter.

00:00:58.725 --> 00:01:00.018 size:84% position:58% line:0%
You have to get the nozzles

00:01:00.018 --> 00:01:03.104 align:end position:100% line:0%
and everything just right
or the flow won't continue.

00:01:03.104 --> 00:01:06.691 align:end position:100% line:0%
It won't pull the liquid
back up through and around.

00:01:06.691 --> 00:01:08.568
So you constantly
have to test it and see,

00:01:08.568 --> 00:01:10.195
and then you have to go back
and adjust it.

00:01:10.528 --> 00:01:11.863
There we go.

00:01:12.447 --> 00:01:14.115
This particular project,

00:01:14.115 --> 00:01:15.700
I've made a couple
of different versions

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:17.494
to see which one would work
best.

00:01:17.494 --> 00:01:18.953
It's not something
I've seen before,

00:01:18.953 --> 00:01:20.538
so it's a little bit
of trial and error,

00:01:20.538 --> 00:01:22.415
and you expect that going in.

00:01:22.415 --> 00:01:23.750
So you try something,
and it's like,

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:25.376
"Well, I should have
made that first."

00:01:25.376 --> 00:01:26.377
So you just do it again.

00:01:26.628 --> 00:01:29.005
This should be spun to this side
over here.

00:01:29.464 --> 00:01:31.633
Being able to physically
hold the thing

00:01:31.633 --> 00:01:33.593
and see it
and look at the sketch

00:01:33.593 --> 00:01:34.844
and then look at the piece
you made

00:01:34.844 --> 00:01:37.847
and it matches and it looks like
what was envisioned, it's

00:01:37.847 --> 00:01:40.433
a really cool process to see
that and actually be like,

00:01:40.433 --> 00:01:41.684
"Okay, I did it right."

00:01:43.561 --> 00:01:46.231
There are less
and less

00:01:46.231 --> 00:01:49.901
opportunities for young
people to learn this craft,

00:01:49.901 --> 00:01:52.195
and so it's really a thrill

00:01:52.195 --> 00:01:54.113
to pass it on to my son.

00:01:54.823 --> 00:01:56.908
It's very rewarding to work
with my father.

00:01:56.908 --> 00:01:59.327
He's taught me so much
and it's cool to be able

00:01:59.327 --> 00:02:01.579
to take what he's taught
me and continue

00:02:01.579 --> 00:02:04.541
to evolve it and then carry
on the legacy in a way.

00:02:05.208 --> 00:02:07.210
Working here with the
researchers and working

00:02:07.210 --> 00:02:10.380
with people that request gifts,
you're real close to

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:12.507
the end user and you get
some immediate feedback.

00:02:13.591 --> 00:02:15.635
When I finish it,
and I know this works well,

00:02:15.844 --> 00:02:17.262
that's going to be
very satisfying.

